<speak>So your objective is to reduce your technology-sector concentration and make your portfolio less sensitive to sharp equity-market movements. Nova Technology Equity Fund is concentrated in technology businesses, so worsening sentiment towards that sector can amplify its declines. Market movements can also change the redemption value before your sale is priced. Do you understand that technology-sector concentration can amplify declines, and that the redemption value can still change before your sale is priced?</speak>